# AIOps Demo Application

Production-like Spring Boot application designed for
observability and AIOps experimentation.

## Endpoints

GET /api/orders
GET /api/orders/{id}

## Failure scenarios

GET /api/orders/high-latency
GET /api/orders/error
GET /api/orders/database-error

## Observability roadmap

Spring Boot
→ OpenTelemetry
→ Prometheus
→ Grafana
→ Elastic
→ PagerDuty
→ RunDeck
→ Kubernetes
→ GenAI

After creating docker image with help of dockerfile

-> image gets created in your local
-> then  run the image in the container
-> docker run -p 8080:8080 aiops-demo:1.0

These are steps to manually start docker and create/spin container and
there is also another way in our springboot app we have compose.yaml file that will automatically create a container
when we hit run the springboot -app everytime

Steps for setting Grafana Email Alert to your email using google/gmail

step1 : Go to https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords

step2 : Google says App Passwords require 2-Step Verification - make it ON first

step3 : new App Password ->
        Name it:    Grafana-LGTM (anyname)
        Copy the 16-character password.Don't put spaces in the App Password
step4: docker stop lgtm  docker rm lgtm
give in your docker container setting like below

docker run -d `
  --name lgtm `
  -p 3000:3000 `
  -p 4317:4317 `
  -p 4318:4318 `
  -v "${PWD}\lgtm-data-backup:/data" `
  -e "GF_SMTP_ENABLED=true" `
  -e "GF_SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com:587" `
  -e "GF_SMTP_USER=YOUR_EMAIL@gmail.com" `
  -e "GF_SMTP_PASSWORD=YOUR_16_CHAR_APP_PASSWORD" `
  -e "GF_SMTP_FROM_ADDRESS=YOUR_EMAIL@gmail.com" `
  -e "GF_SMTP_FROM_NAME=Grafana Observability" `
  -e "GF_SMTP_SKIP_VERIFY=false" `
  -e "GF_SMTP_EHLO_IDENTITY=localhost" `
  grafana/otel-lgtm:latest


step5: Verify Docker received it

docker exec lgtm sh -c 'echo "USER=$GF_SMTP_USER"; echo "PASSWORD_LENGTH=${#GF_SMTP_PASSWORD}"; echo "HOST=$GF_SMTP_HOST"'


USER=yourgmail@gmail.com
PASSWORD_LENGTH=16
HOST=smtp.gmail.com:587


step 6: Test Grafana

Open:

http://localhost:3000
Go to:   Alerting → Contact points
Then:    Your email contact point → Test
Click:    Send test notification